      "updated_at": "2018-01-28T21:05:16Z",
      "body": "I agree that GDPR compliance itself is critical (we've started reviewing our own systems like SilverStripe Platform and silverstripe.com/org back in November). But in the context of our open source software, my understaning is that the software itself is neither a \"Data Processor\" nor a \"Data Controller\". It really depends on what you build with it. I agree that some documentation about potential privacy impacts emerging from our software would be nice. But unless somebody thinks we need to change our APIs or system behaviour, it's not `impact/critical`. I'll raise a GDPR blog post with our marketing team! :)",
      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "pin": null,
